  "id": "emotional-divorce",
  "term": "emotional divorce",
  "definition": "Emotional divorce is a state in which spouses continue living together and carrying out marital roles, but are effectively separated in emotional and relational ways. It is marked by distance, lack of intimacy, and reduced love, trust, respect, or concern between partners, and it has been linked with poorer mental health such as greater depression, anxiety, and loneliness.",
